Description: Bayesian exponential smoothing (ETS) state space models for
    univariate time series, accounting for both parameter and model
    uncertainty. The initial states and the error variance are integrated out
    analytically, under a conjugate Normal-inverse-chi-squared prior; the
    smoothing parameters are integrated numerically, by adaptive Gauss-Hermite
    quadrature (AGHQ) or adaptive importance sampling (AIS). 
    The ETS models are combined by Bayesian model averaging (BMA), and forecasts are obtained 
    by simulating future sample paths. 
    Currently only additive models are supported.
